    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Decision error mapping" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolResults.cs">Extend, do not fork: the general error record is the base, DecisionToolError maps to it</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate (gh pr view 3161 --json state; r1 TASK-INDEX 042 done); merge origin/master into this branch; build.</step>
    <step order="2">Generalise McpToolResults; run the r1 MCP contract and auth suites unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">Add McpLongRunning and McpLongRunningTests (start shape, status shapes, link built by the helper).</step>
    <step order="4">Split the ledger into per-area partial files; add the must-fire/must-not-fire guard proof; run Spaarke.ArchTests.</step>
    <step order="5">Clear the DecisionsTextSummary.cs comment; update HOW-TO-ADD-AN-MCP-TOOL.md; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the r1 gate is not met, STOP; do not start.</trigger>
    <trigger>If keeping decision-tool error bytes identical is impossible with a general type, STOP and escalate (r1 contract).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>McpToolResults.FromError (r1) handles DecisionToolError only; the legacy agent's start/poll (AgentEndpoints.cs:461-481, PlaybookStatusEndpoints.cs, deleted by 001) is the only prior start/status shape; CAPABILITY-INDEX has no MCP long-running row.</existing>
    <extension>McpToolResults is extended in place. The start/status helper is new because no live code builds an MCP start/status result; it is a static builder of two result shapes, not a service, so no DI registration.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Each long-running tool (030, 032, 034) would invent its own start/status shape and error mapping, breaking FR-14's "the pattern is shared code" acceptance; without the ledger split, parallel tool tasks conflict on one array.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/; dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests; MCP contract and auth suites</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolResults.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpLongRunning.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.*.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpToolResultsGeneralTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpLongRunningTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/HOW-TO-ADD-AN-MCP-TOOL.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">All r1 MCP tests (contract/Api/Mcp, auth/Mcp, Mcp.Conformance.Host) pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">McpToolResultsGeneralTests: a general error produces isError with structuredContent { reasonCode, message, status, correlationId }; a decision error produces the same bytes as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">McpLongRunningTests: Started returns { runId, status, consoleLink } with the helper-built link; Status returns each of queued/running/completed/failed with optional progress/result.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (must-fire): a tool class absent from every ledger partial fails the guard; must-not-fire: every r1 tool passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">git grep -i "api/agent" -- src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp returns nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build 0 warnings; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-14, Tools. uac-r2 reviews the ledger restructure. Later tool tasks each own one ledger partial.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
